      "B": "Definitely! They were asked to share their experiences with others. Not only ordinary people but also philosophers were in close contact with them to learn more about the condition.",
      "C": "Well, they had been thought to have supernatural powers until medical science clearly defined the characteristics of the condition and detected its prevalence.",
      "D": "As far as I know, synesthesia was not regarded as a serious subject for decades. A major factor for such late attention was that people were thought to be highly emotional and poetic rather than having a particular condition.",
      "E": "After all, someone with this condition can experience feelings others are deprived of in their lives. I'm not certain but it must have been the same for those in the past."
