      "C": "As aloe vera was initially grown on the Arabian Peninsula, the fact that its leaves contain antioxidants crucial to healthy skin was first discovered there, but later it became a global botanical product.",
      "D": "The leaves of aloe vera contain antioxidants that are vital to healthy skin, which boosts its global recognition as a botanical product, yet it was the Arabian Peninsula which first grew it considering its benefits.",
      "E": "Before aloe vera became a botanical product used throughout the entire world, it had initially been grown on the Arabian Peninsula, where its leaves involving antioxidants were used to ensure healthy skin."
